# Demo protocol. Prerequisites: both channels connected (server panel has a client,
# client panel is connected to some server). Then press "Start protocol".
#
# Syntax (one command per line, # starts a comment):
#   encoding UTF-8|ASCII           how "strings" become bytes (default UTF-8)
#   timeout 5s                     default wait for every expect (ms | s | m)
#   pause 2s
#   client|server send "text"      escapes: \n \r \t \0 \\ \" \xNN (raw byte)
#   client|server send hex 02 41 03
#   client|server expect "text"    buffer must START with text; only that is consumed
#   client|server expect contains "text"
#   client|server expect /regex/   whole buffered text must match
#   client|server expect hex 41 42
#   client|server expect any
#   ... expect ... timeout 10s     per-step timeout
#   client|server close

encoding UTF-8
timeout 30s

client send    "A"
client expect  "B"
pause 2s
server expect  "C"
server send    "D"
server expect  /^HELLO \d+$/
client expect  contains "OK"
client send    "line1\r\nline2\x00"
client send    hex 02 41 42 03
client expect  any timeout 5s
client close
